 "transcript": [
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Bosch HBS534BS0B oven displaying E011 and won't let me do anything. Beeping. Help!"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "E011 on Bosch ovens is ambiguous; it typically indicates either a temperature sensor fault or a control panel issue (like a stuck button). A stuck button or faulty membrane is a strong possibility. Please press each button individually to see if any feel different. If all buttons feel normal, we will look at the internal wiring for the temperature sensor."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "I can't really press them with it beeping and not accepting input. None of the buttons look damaged though. It started about an hour ago right after I wiped the panel with a wet cloth and a kitchen spray, if that helps."
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "The fact that this started immediately after using a wet cloth and spray suggests moisture has seeped into the control panel, causing a short circuit or 'stuck' signal. This is a common issue with these touch controls. To help clear any residual charge or dry out minor condensation, please switch off the oven at the wall (using the cooker switch or fuse box), wait 5 minutes, then switch it back on. Does the beeping and error code clear?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Done that, switched off at the cooker switch for 5 minutes after drying the panel with a towel. It's come back up normally with no code. Heated to 180C fine too. Is that it?"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "Yes, that is it. To prevent this happening again, please avoid spraying cleaners directly onto the oven fascia; instead, spray your cloth first and then wipe the controls. If you ever see E011 return without any recent cleaning, let me know."
  }
 ],
